# Development and runtime environments

- Assume the developer host is Windows with PowerShell 7 unless stated otherwise.
- Label local examples as PowerShell. Use Windows paths and PowerShell syntax there.
- Use Git Bash only for an explicitly labeled POSIX-compatible local command;
  Git Bash is useful compatibility, not proof that code works on Linux.
- Assume Sprites and deployed workers run Linux with Bash, case-sensitive paths,
  forward slashes, and no Windows drive letters or `.cmd` executables.
- Keep text UTF-8 without BOM. Linux/runtime files use LF; Windows-only
  `.ps1`, `.cmd`, and `.bat` files use CRLF.
- Prefer TypeScript/Python and platform path/process APIs over shell-specific glue.
- Verify local host behavior on Windows and runtime behavior on Linux or CI.
- Read `docs/development-environments.md` before adding scripts or setup commands.
